  "full_response": "### **Design Patterns**\nDesign patterns are reusable, well-proven solutions to common problems in software design. They provide best practices for structuring code to improve maintainability, scalability, and flexibility. Design patterns are categorized into three main types:\n\n1. **Creational Patterns** – Deal with object creation mechanisms.\n2. **Structural Patterns** – Focus on class and object composition.\n3. **Behavioral Patterns** – Define communication between objects.\n\n---\n\n## **1. Observer Pattern (Behavioral)**\n**Purpose:** Defines a one-to-many dependency between objects so that when one object (the **subject**) changes state, all its dependents (**observers**) are notified and updated automatically.\n\n### **Key Components:**\n- **Subject (Observable):** Maintains a list of observers and provides methods to attach/detach them.\n- **Observer:** Defines an update interface for objects that should be notified of changes.\n- **Concrete Subject:** Implements the subject and sends notifications to observers.\n- **Concrete Observer:** Implements the observer interface and reacts to updates.\n\n### **Example Use Cases:**\n- Event handling systems (e.g., GUI buttons, stock market updates).\n- Publish-subscribe systems (e.g., news feeds, messaging apps).\n\n### **Example (Java-like Pseudocode):**\n```java\n// Subject (Observable)\nclass NewsAgency {\n    private List<NewsChannel> channels = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    public void addObserver(NewsChannel channel) {\n        channels.add(channel);\n    }\n\n    public void removeObserver(NewsChannel channel) {\n        channels.remove(channel);\n    }\n\n    public void setNews(String news) {\n        for (NewsChannel channel : channels) {\n            channel.update(news);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Observer\ninterface NewsChannel {\n    void update(String news);\n}\n\n// Concrete Observer\nclass NewsChannelImpl implements NewsChannel {\n    private String news;\n\n    @Override\n    public void update(String news) {\n        this.news = news;\n        System.out.println(\"Breaking News: \" + news);\n    }\n}\n\n// Usage\nNewsAgency agency = new NewsAgency();\nNewsChannel channel1 = new NewsChannelImpl();\nNewsChannel channel2 = new NewsChannelImpl();\n\nagency.addObserver(channel1);\nagency.addObserver(channel2);\n\nagency.setNews(\"New AI breakthrough announced!\");\n// Output:\n// Breaking News: New AI breakthrough announced!\n// Breaking News: New AI breakthrough announced!\n```\n\n---\n\n## **2. Factory Pattern (Creational",
